Personal Mini-Toolkit

Project Description

The Personal Mini-Toolkit is a Python command-line application developed as part of the Power Learn Project (PLP) Week 8 final project.

It combines three useful Python tools into one program. Users can select a tool from a menu and interact with it until they choose to quit.

Tools Included

1. Simple Calculator

- Performs addition
- Performs subtraction
- Performs multiplication
- Performs division
- Handles division by zero and invalid number inputs

2. To-Do List Manager

- Allows users to add tasks
- Displays all saved tasks
- Allows users to remove tasks
- Handles empty lists and invalid task numbers

3. Number Guessing Game

- Generates a random number between 1 and 20
- Allows users to guess the number
- Gives hints when a guess is too high or too low
- Counts the number of attempts

Python Concepts Used

This project demonstrates the use of:

- Variables and data types
- Lists and list methods
- While loops
- For loops
- Conditional statements ("if", "elif", and "else")
- User input and output
- Functions and the "random" module
- Exception handling using "try" and "except"
- F-strings
- Comments

How to Run the Program

1. Make sure Python 3 is installed.
2. Download or clone this repository.
3. Open the project folder in a Python environment.
4. Run the following command:

python toolkit.py

The program will display a menu where you can choose which tool to use.

The program can also be run using Pydroid 3 on Android.

Screenshots

The "screenshots" folder contains images showing:

