Project Reflection

The most challenging part of this project was bringing all three tools together in one program using a menu loop. I also had to understand how nested loops work, especially in the To-Do List Manager and Number Guessing Game. One of the main issues I had to handle was preventing invalid user inputs from stopping the program. Testing each tool helped me identify and correct errors. I learned how to use lists, loops, conditionals, exception handling, and the random module in a practical project. If I had one more week, I would improve the toolkit by adding a feature to save tasks permanently so that they are still available when the program is restarted.

